INT. TRANSPORT CAFE - NIGHT

Rain hammers the window. JUNE, 40s, sits with a cold coffee and a
folded map. The door bangs. MARCO, 30s, soaked, drops into the seat
opposite without asking.

MARCO
You said six.

JUNE
I said I would try for six.

She does not look up from the map.

MARCO
(quieter)
The yard is empty. Everything is gone.

JUNE
Then we were right.

MARCO
That is not the comfort you think it is.

June folds the map, once, twice, and puts it in her coat.

JUNE
Drink something. We leave in ten minutes.
